P-005.falsifiable_test:
1. Report val rel_l2 overall and the per-parameter relative RMSE.
2. Compare against the init-only MLP (the same model before refinement) and against a mode readout (estimator=mode) under the same LM settings.
3. The hypothesis is falsified if any of these holds:
   - val rel_l2 >= 0.03;
   - posterior_mean is not better than mode;
   - more than 2% of samples show final residual chi^2/dof > 2, which would indicate initializer failure or local minima.

P-013.response_to_critic:
Point-by-point responses.

(1) r/sigma is largely settled by P-002. Accepted. P-002's residual at truth (about 0.000995) is treated as establishing that the train features carry one noise draw. r/sigma is kept only as an internal check that this solver's reshape matches the harness layout. A value of about 1 confirms the regenerated clean traces are used. A value above 3 triggers the fallback, and the arm then becomes a no-augmentation control.

(2) Overlap with P-012. Accepted. P-011 is now explicitly cell B, 'real-clean+fresh, n_sim=0', of the shared factorial {A: real-noisy, B: real-clean+fresh, C: +6000 sim, D: +12000 sim}. I fix and publish the canonical model so P-012 can reuse it verbatim:
